Add a "PHP Baremetal" table to phpinfo().

A second table right under phpinfo()'s general table: the project name, the board, the firmware
version (PROJECT_VER) and the ESP-IDF version. The phpbm firmware sets them as C globals in
boot.c (phpbm_project, phpbm_board, phpbm_version, phpbm_idf_version), so they stay out of the
environment.

--- a/ext/standard/info.c
+++ b/ext/standard/info.c
@@ -907,6 +907,18 @@
 
 		php_info_print_table_end();
 
+		/* PHP Baremetal: project, board and versions, set by the phpbm firmware (boot.c). */
+		{
+			extern const char *phpbm_project, *phpbm_board, *phpbm_version, *phpbm_idf_version;
+			php_info_print_table_start();
+			php_info_print_table_colspan_header(2, "PHP Baremetal");
+			php_info_print_table_row(2, "Project", phpbm_project);
+			php_info_print_table_row(2, "Board", phpbm_board);
+			php_info_print_table_row(2, "Firmware version", phpbm_version);
+			php_info_print_table_row(2, "ESP-IDF", phpbm_idf_version);
+			php_info_print_table_end();
+		}
+
 		/* Zend Engine */
 		php_info_print_box_start(0);
 		if (!sapi_module.phpinfo_as_text) {
